WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.024
Scrooge awoke to a bright light. In front of him was a strange old man.

2
00:00:06.025 --> 00:00:12.947
In some ways he looked ancient, but he had young, childlike features and was dressed in summer flowers.

3
00:00:12.948 --> 00:00:20.704
"Are you the first ghost that Marley predicted?" asked Scrooge.

4
00:00:20.705 --> 00:00:26.568
"Yes, I am the Ghost of Christmas Past," replied the ghost.

5
00:00:26.569 --> 00:00:35.333
"Tonight you will see images of your past, but they will have no awareness of us. Come with me!"

6
00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:41.690
The ghost kindly took Scrooge's hand and walked into the past.

7
00:00:41.691 --> 00:00:49.612
Scrooge could hear his old employer, Mr. Fezziwig, yelling out, "Ebenezer! Dick! Come here, boys.

8
00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:53.002
No more work for today. It's Christmas Eve.

9
00:00:53.003 --> 00:00:55.990
Give me a hand and let's clear away the desks for a party."

10
00:00:55.991 --> 00:01:02.084
Old Scrooge could not believe how young and happy he used to look.

11
00:01:02.085 --> 00:01:04.281
Well, it was a grand party.

12
00:01:04.282 --> 00:01:09.863
Mrs. Fezziwig, the cook, and the maid came in with food and drinks for everyone.

13
00:01:09.864 --> 00:01:14.495
Then the rest of the men and women who worked for the company were invited.

14
00:01:14.496 --> 00:01:17.024
They had a dance and a feast.

15
00:01:17.025 --> 00:01:22.664
Scrooge danced with the prettiest girl all night.

16
00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:27.126
Old Scrooge shed a tear as he remembered the happy old days.

17
00:01:27.127 --> 00:01:31.621
"We must move on," said the Ghost of Christmas Past.

18
00:01:31.622 --> 00:01:36.602
"Can't I just have a few more minutes?" pleaded Scrooge.

19
00:01:36.603 --> 00:01:41.033
"I'm sorry," replied the ghost.

20
00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:46.881
Then Scrooge saw himself a little older, sitting with the girl who he had danced with.

21
00:01:46.882 --> 00:01:51.254
Crying, she said, "You have another love now."

22
00:01:51.255 --> 00:01:55.854
"No," replied Scrooge. "You are the only woman."

23
00:01:55.855 --> 00:02:00.968
"It's not a woman you love. It's gold you love," she said.

24
00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:05.655
"So, go to your true love."

25
00:02:05.656 --> 00:02:11.451
Angrily, old Scrooge shouted, "Get me out of this place. Take me back!"

26
00:02:11.452 --> 00:02:15.609
The ghost nodded, and Scrooge was again sleeping in his bed.

27
00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:23.037
But it seemed only minutes later that Scrooge was awoken by a bright light from his living room.

28
00:02:23.038 --> 00:02:26.088
In the room, a fire was burning brightly.

29
00:02:26.089 --> 00:02:30.935
Sitting by the fire was a jolly ghost, eating meat and drinking wine.

30
00:02:30.936 --> 00:02:36.895
"Come join me," he called. "I am the Ghost of Christmas Present."

31
00:02:36.896 --> 00:02:39.822
"Lead me, spirit," said Scrooge.

32
00:02:39.823 --> 00:02:46.732
"Tonight I have learned many things. I'm sure you will teach me more."

33
00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:50.188
"Touch my robe," replied the ghost.

34
00:02:50.189 --> 00:02:56.385
Immediately Scrooge and the ghost left the house and were standing in Bob Cratchit's tiny living room.

35
00:02:56.386 --> 00:02:58.749
Scrooge counted four children.

36
00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:05.272
"How does Bob feed them all on his salary?" Scrooge wondered aloud.

37
00:03:05.273 --> 00:03:09.272
Mrs. Cratchit was dressed in a poor and simple dress.

38
00:03:09.273 --> 00:03:16.249
But she had a smile as she cooked the Christmas turkey, prepared the gravy, and dished out the applesauce.

39
00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:23.172
"Where is your father?" she asked. "Church should be finished by now."

40
00:03:23.173 --> 00:03:27.685
"Here he comes," shouted four children at once.

41
00:03:27.686 --> 00:03:31.105
In came Bob Cratchit carrying Tiny Tim.

42
00:03:31.106 --> 00:03:35.488
Tiny Tim was very sick, and his legs never did work.

43
00:03:35.489 --> 00:03:41.111
But Bob loved him because he had a gentle heart.

44
00:03:41.112 --> 00:03:44.714
Soon all seven were seated and ready to eat.

45
00:03:44.715 --> 00:03:48.518
Scrooge had never seen such a warm and loving sight.

46
00:03:48.519 --> 00:03:58.010
Even though their clothes were nearly rags and their house was humble, it was the most handsome family Scrooge had ever seen.

47
00:03:58.011 --> 00:04:05.717
At the end of the meal, Bob raised his glass, saying, "A Merry Christmas to all of us! God bless us!"

48
00:04:05.718 --> 00:04:09.887
Then Tiny Tim repeated, "God bless everyone."

49
00:04:09.888 --> 00:04:17.537
Surprising Scrooge, Bob said, "To Mr. Scrooge, who gave us the money for this meal."

50
00:04:17.538 --> 00:04:23.908
"Mr. Scrooge? No," replied his wife. "He gives us almost nothing."

51
00:04:23.909 --> 00:04:28.478
Bob looked sternly at his wife and said, "It's Christmas."

52
00:04:28.479 --> 00:04:33.765
"Fine," said his wife more politely. "To Mr. Scrooge."

53
00:04:33.766 --> 00:04:39.785
At that, the ghost touched Scrooge, and they were in another house.

54
00:04:39.786 --> 00:04:43.972
He could hear the laughter of his nephew.

55
00:04:43.973 --> 00:04:48.820
"He said that Christmas was a humbug!" cried Scrooge's nephew.

56
00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:52.296
"Shame on him," declared his pretty wife.

57
00:04:52.297 --> 00:05:01.720
"How terrible of him to be rude to you when you were trying to be kind to him."

58
00:05:01.721 --> 00:05:05.631
"Well, it only hurts him," replied Scrooge's nephew.

59
00:05:05.632 --> 00:05:10.452
"Here we sit with each other and good food, and he is in his lonely house.

60
00:05:10.453 --> 00:05:12.285
I feel sorry for him."

61
00:05:12.286 --> 00:05:17.429
"Well, don't!" exclaimed his wife. "'Bah! Humbug!' to him."

62
00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.820
And they laughed. Even old Scrooge laughed.

63
00:05:20.821 --> 00:05:26.372
He was a humbug, but he would change.

64
00:05:26.373 --> 00:05:32.072
Then the scene faded, and the Ghost of Christmas Present flew him all over the city.

65
00:05:32.073 --> 00:05:37.172
They went to hospitals and workhouses and saw children suffering.

66
00:05:37.173 --> 00:05:49.582
In the streets they saw men and women freezing, but in the jails they saw the worst misery of all.

